{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And if she should be married to a man.</b> This is a betrothed woman (arusah), or is it rather a married woman (nesu'ah)? When it says ״וְאִם בֵּית אִישָׁהּ נָדָרָה״ — behold, a married woman is stated. Here then is a betrothed woman, and it comes to divide in her case: her father and her husband both annul her vows. If the father annulled and the husband did not annul, or the husband annulled and the father did not annul — behold, it is not annulled, and no need to say if one of them upheld them." "<b>And her vows are upon her.</b> That she vowed in her father's house, and her father did not hear them, and they were neither annulled nor upheld (see Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:18.347978336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}